{"kind":"promise","text":"Claude promises c60a3a97, the contradictory promise-only completion guidance on the gs state and MCP ratify reference pages, on request/direct-report-reference-clarity from main 32660749. Second of the two refiles I asked for in 6ac149e7, replacing the stale d52a6b1b, whose promise I treat as released by author replacement rather than completed. I will take it after the record guide correction, as the request directs.\n\nThe defect is that one paragraph says every report requires an effective promise while the next permits reporting against the request, and the MCP page describes the originating request only through a promise, so a reader finishing already-done work can conclude they must manufacture a promise first. The shipped boundary is narrower and worth stating exactly: a direct report is admitted only from the request's addressee, and is refused while that reporter holds a live effective promise on the request; otherwise the report closes the promise it cites, and the fold resolves the originating request for either shape. I will make the guidance internally consistent and explicit about both existing paths, say who may report and when the live promise must be used, and say how the originating requester accepts a non-merge report on either path. The adjacent artifact paragraph will be corrected only so far as it implies direct assigned implementation is impossible. I will never suggest withdrawing a live promise to bypass it, and independent exact-head review with sealed-merge closure and no extra implementation ratification stays as it is.\n\nI will verify the walkthroughs against real current behaviour rather than paraphrasing: an addressee with no promise reporting successfully, a stranger refused, an existing live promise closed through itself, the originating requester accepting the direct non-merge report, and direct implementation still proceeding through artifact, review and sealed merge. Existing focused tests and the documentation gates, not new tests mirroring wording. Short linked explanations rather than duplicating the lifecycle across both pages.\n\nScope stays docs/reference/gs/state.md and docs/reference/mcp/ratify.md plus only a directly necessary link or provenance correction, with the event-identifier page, the record-guide wording and the AGENTS and SKILL editorial work left to the requests that own them. No runtime, schema, workflow-state, authority, API, service or dependency change. Provenance published on current behaviour artifacts at each exact changed path, independent Architecture, Security and Simplification review at the exact head, ratification, sealed landing, push of main and the workroom ref, CI verified, worktree and branch removed.","body":{"branch":"request/direct-report-reference-clarity","request":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:057341d5a07e41cb025ee0fd5de2c674c60a3a97"}}